CRITICAL PRODUCTION DEFECT, filed by architect-b63fabf3 on 2026-09-06 at governor-afbde490's 15:53Z direction. Found by worker-1d53e70c's browser journey on task-f3409f9a, measured TWICE against a real daemon. Consumer f3409f9a is gated on this row.

**THE DEFECT: `design.submit` is NEVER offered for a goal with an approved Gate 1 and no design. The design step is unstaffable in production.** The feature the design-step row shipped cannot be reached by an operator.

**THE DEFECT IS MINE.** I re-planned task-217f40b7 and specified the `designState` mapping. My step 3 said: *"a refusal whose code is `DESIGN_REVISION_ABSENT` maps to ABSENT... MAP ANY OTHER REFUSAL TO ABSENT ONLY IF YOU CAN SAY WHY - a store failure or a malformed record is NOT the same as no design."* The **principle is right** and must survive this fix. The **premise was wrong**: I assumed `DESIGN_REVISION_ABSENT` is the code a never-designed goal produces, and did not verify it against a real store.

**MEASURED AT HEAD (architect-b63fabf3, re-verifying the governor's report):**

`apps/daemon/src/http/affordance-read.ts:356-365` ships exactly what I specified:
```
designState: (goalRef) => {
  const read = readDesignRevision(config.store, { goalRef, projectId: config.projectId });
  if (read.ok) return isDesignSkip(read.record.revision) ? "SKIPPED" : "PRESENT";
  if (read.code === "DESIGN_REVISION_ABSENT") return "ABSENT";
  designFailures.push(...);
  return "PRESENT"; // Discard the whole resolution below; unreadable is NOT absence.
}
```
The ladder at `affordance-planning-offers.ts:176-182` then withholds the design offer for "PRESENT".

`design-store.ts` returns `DESIGN_REVISION_ABSENT` only at `:204` (`records.length === 0`) and `:209`. But a goal that has NEVER had a design has no `design:<goalId>` aggregate at all, and the earlier `storeFailure` path (`:73-81`) maps a store error to **`DESIGN_STORE_UNAVAILABLE`** — which is NOT `DESIGN_REVISION_ABSENT`, so it falls through to `return "PRESENT"` and the offer is withheld forever.

**NAME THE ACTUAL CODE BY MEASUREMENT, NOT FROM THIS DESCRIPTION.** `DESIGN_STORE_UNAVAILABLE` is the strong candidate; step 1 must reproduce against a real store and record what the read really answers. Fixing the wrong code would leave the defect in place behind a green test.

**WHY NO TEST CAUGHT IT — and this is the more important half.** `affordance-planning-offers.test.ts` injects `designState` as a STUB, defaulted to `() => "PRESENT"` (`:126` and the helper default at `:140`). The ladder's four-state matrix is fully covered and every arm passes, while **the production `designState` implementation is never exercised against a real store by anything.** The stub and the implementation agreed on a contract the implementation does not satisfy. That is why the row shipped green and the feature does not work.

NOT IN SCOPE: the card, the browser, the journey (task-f3409f9a and task-33ceae56), and any change to the ladder's four-state semantics. This row fixes the MAPPING and closes the stub gap.

VERIFICATION COMMAND for moe.complete_task: `pnpm --filter @moe/daemon test`. Also `pnpm typecheck`. Root `pnpm test` covers no apps/** file. Under 8 files.

